{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 27, :comments ["<b>And the princes brought.</b> Rabbi Natan said: What did the princes see to donate at the dedication of the altar first, but at the work of the Tabernacle they did not donate first? Rather, thus the princes said: Let the congregation donate what they donate, and whatever they lack — we complete it. Once the congregation completed everything — as it says ״וְהַמְּלָאכָה הָיְתָה דַיָּם״ (Exodus 36:7) — the princes said: What is upon us to do? <b>They brought the shoham stones,</b> etc. Therefore they donated at the dedication of the altar first. And because they held back at the beginning, a letter was missing from their name — and וְהַנְּשִׂאִם is written (without the yod) (Sifrei Numbers 45)."], :book :exodus, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 35, :notes {}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T08:56:45.625971479Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}